  "applies": true,
  "fixmes": [],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Applies.** `validate_rust_functions` in `src/rust_coverage.rs` is a repository-validation function with a parameter named `errors: &mut Vec<String>`. It collects validation errors and does not abort on them, so it is a site of `requirements.ci.errors`. The site's obligations are:\n- It keeps running later checks that don't depend on a failed check's result, including within the same loop iteration.\n- It doesn't report one failure twice.\n\n**The `continue` at line 245 is harmless.**\n- It sits in the `Err` arm of `fs::read_to_string(&file)`. That arm pushes a \"cannot read Rust source\" error to `errors` (and to `discovery_errors`), then moves on to the next file.\n- The only later check in the iteration is `missing_function_references(&source, definitions)`. It takes the file's text as input, so it depends on the read that failed. Skipping it is correct.\n- The loop does continue to every remaining file, so one unreadable file doesn't stop the other files' read, parse and citation-coverage checks.\n- The parse failure arm (`Err(error)` from `missing_function_references`) does not exit early. It records the error and the loop proceeds.\n- Missing citations are all pushed in a `for` loop with no exit.\n\n**No double reporting at this site.**\n- Each failure is formatted once and pushed once to `errors`. The same string is also cloned into `discovery_errors`, but that is a separate channel. `inspect_repository_with_progress` (`src/evidence.rs`) returns it as `RepositoryInspection.discovery_errors`, while the validation report's `errors` is a different vector.\n- An unreadable `.rs` file can also get a \"cannot read reference source\" error from `collect_references_with_progress`. That error comes from a different check (reference discovery) with a different message. I treated it as that check's own failure, not a repeat inside this site.\n\n**Gaps:** none.",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "file": "src/rust_coverage.rs",
      "item": "fn[validate_rust_functions]",
      "hash": "4153358d65ac0e56d727e87689e3ce1f0c2f4e4bf223c3f5513b87cf49fbeac7"
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.ci.errors",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.ci.errors"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::::{req} errors",
        "Repository validation MUST continue after a failed check and report every failed",
        "check it finds in one run, each as a {term}`requirements.ci.validation_error`.",
        "This is a convention for every validation error; the requirement for each check",
        "states which conditions that check reports. A file that cannot be parsed, such as",
        "a malformed `habeas.toml`, `book.toml`, or evidence file, is one failed check:",
        "its error MAY report only the first parse or decoding problem in that file, and",
        "checks that do not depend on its contents MUST still run.",
        "",
        "The code that sequences the repository's checks carries out the first paragraph.",
        "A repository-validation function that collects validation errors MUST hold them",
        "in a parameter or local variable named `errors`, and a function with such a",
        "variable is a site below; authoring code that collects errors only to abort is",
        "not one. After one of its checks fails, a site MUST still run every later check",
        "that does not depend on the failed check's result, including later checks in the",
        "same loop iteration, and MUST NOT report one failure twice.",
        "",
        "::::{sites} error_accumulators",
        "```yaml",
        "language: rust",
        "paths: [src]",
        "exclude: [src/authoring/inputs.rs, src/authoring/tools.rs]",
        "rule:",
        "  kind: function_item",
        "  has:",
        "    stopBy: { kind: function_item }",
        "    any:",
        "      - kind: parameter",
        "        has: { field: pattern, regex: \"^errors$\" }",
        "      - kind: let_declaration",
        "        has: { field: pattern, regex: \"^errors$\" }",
        "  not:",
        "    inside:",
        "      stopBy: end",
        "      kind: mod_item",
        "      has: { field: name, regex: \"^tests$\" }",
        "match:",
        "  - \"fn check(value: &str, errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}\"",
        "  - |",
        "    fn run() {",
        "        let mut errors: BTreeSet<String> = BTreeSet::new();",
        "        check(\"\", &mut errors);",
        "    }",
        "no_match:",
        "  - \"fn check(value: &str, discovery_errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}\"",
        "  - |",
        "    fn run() {",
        "        let mut problems = Vec::new();",
        "        check(\"\", &mut problems);",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    mod tests {",
        "        fn check(errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}",
        "    }",
        "```",
        "::::",
        "",
        "::::{violations} early_exits",
        "```yaml",
        "language: rust",
        "paths: [src]",
        "within: error_accumulators",
        "rule:",
        "  any:",
        "    - kind: try_expression",
        "    - kind: return_expression",
        "    - kind: continue_expression",
        "    - kind: break_expression",
        "match:",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(v: &Value, errors: &mut Vec<String>) -> Option<u8> {",
        "        let n = v.as_u64()?;",
        "        if v.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "        Some(n as u8)",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(items: &[Value], errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        for item in items {",
        "            if !item.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); continue; }",
        "            if item.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "        }",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(v: &Value, errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        if !v.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); return; }",
        "        if v.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(items: &[Value], errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        for item in items {",
        "            if !item.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); break; }",
        "        }",
        "        if items.is_empty() { errors.push(\"empty\".into()); }",
        "    }",
        "no_match:",
        "  - |",
        "    fn parse(v: &Value) -> Option<u8> {",
        "        let n = v.as_u64()?;",
        "        Some(n as u8)",
        "    }",
        "```",
        "::::",
        ":::::"
      ]
    },
